sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Browser as Browser client
    participant API as Axum API process
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Publisher as Outbox publisher
    participant Kafka as Kafka orders topic
    participant Inventory as Inventory consumer group
    participant Fulfillment as Fulfillment consumer group
    participant Notifications as Notifications consumer group

    Note over Browser,Notifications: One possible successful execution, not a globally synchronized timeline.

    Browser->>API: POST /api/v1/orders with idempotency key
    API->>DB: Commit pending order, items, and OrderCreated outbox row
    DB-->>API: Order committed
    API-->>Browser: 201 pending and Location

    Publisher->>DB: Poll oldest unpublished event
    DB-->>Publisher: OrderCreated outbox row
    Publisher->>Kafka: Publish OrderCreated
    Publisher->>DB: Mark outbox row published after acknowledgement
    Kafka-->>Inventory: Deliver OrderCreated
    Inventory->>DB: Deduplicate, lock product rows, check stock
    alt Enough stock
        Inventory->>DB: Reserve stock, accept order, enqueue OrderAccepted
        DB-->>Inventory: Transaction committed
        Inventory->>Kafka: Commit OrderCreated record offset
        Publisher->>DB: Poll next unpublished event
        DB-->>Publisher: OrderAccepted outbox row
        Publisher->>Kafka: Publish OrderAccepted
        Publisher->>DB: Mark outbox row published after acknowledgement
        par Fulfillment and OrderShipped publication
            Kafka-->>Fulfillment: Deliver OrderAccepted
            Fulfillment->>DB: Create simulated shipment, mark shipped, enqueue OrderShipped
            DB-->>Fulfillment: Shipment transaction committed
            Fulfillment->>Kafka: Commit OrderAccepted record offset
            Publisher->>DB: Poll next unpublished event
            DB-->>Publisher: OrderShipped outbox row
            Publisher->>Kafka: Publish OrderShipped
            Publisher->>DB: Mark outbox row published after acknowledgement
        and Notifications handle acceptance independently
            Kafka-->>Notifications: Deliver OrderAccepted
            Notifications->>DB: Insert accepted notification and dedupe marker
            DB-->>Notifications: Notification transaction committed
            Notifications->>Kafka: Commit OrderAccepted record offset
        end
        par Browser reads order history
            Browser->>API: GET /api/v1/customers/{customer_id}/orders?limit=20&offset=0
            API->>DB: Read order history
            DB-->>API: Shipped order
            API-->>Browser: Show shipped status
        and Browser reads notifications separately
            Browser->>API: GET /api/v1/customers/{customer_id}/notifications?limit=20&offset=0
            API->>DB: Read current notification rows
            DB-->>API: Notifications available so far
            API-->>Browser: Show current notifications
        end
        Kafka-->>Notifications: Deliver OrderShipped independently
        Notifications->>DB: Insert shipped notification and dedupe marker
        DB-->>Notifications: Notification transaction committed
        Notifications->>Kafka: Commit OrderShipped record offset
        Note over Browser,Notifications: Order history and notifications are separate reads.<br/>The browser may see shipped status before its notification appears.
        Note over Publisher,Notifications: Fulfillment and notifications run in independent consumer groups.<br/>Publishing OrderShipped does not wait for acceptance notification creation<br/>or for the notifications consumer to commit its offset.
    else Insufficient stock
        Inventory->>DB: Leave stock unchanged, reject order, enqueue OrderRejected
        DB-->>Inventory: Rejection transaction committed
        Inventory->>Kafka: Commit OrderCreated record offset
        Publisher->>DB: Poll next unpublished event
        DB-->>Publisher: OrderRejected outbox row
        Publisher->>Kafka: Publish OrderRejected
        Publisher->>DB: Mark outbox row published after acknowledgement
        Kafka-->>Notifications: Deliver OrderRejected independently
        Notifications->>DB: Insert rejection notification and dedupe marker
        DB-->>Notifications: Notification transaction committed
        Notifications->>Kafka: Commit OrderRejected record offset
        Browser->>API: GET /api/v1/customers/{customer_id}/orders
        API->>DB: Read order history
        DB-->>API: Rejected order
        API-->>Browser: Show rejected status
        Browser->>API: GET /api/v1/customers/{customer_id}/notifications
        API->>DB: Read notification rows separately
        DB-->>API: Rejection notification
        API-->>Browser: Show rejection notification
    end
